    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 9,
    "summary": "Job acknowledges the justice and greatness of God and concludes that man cannot contend against Him.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Then Job answered and said,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 9:1",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 9,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "I know it is so of a truth: but how should man be just with God?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 55,
            "end": 59,
            "text": "IE before."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 7,
            "end": 12
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 9:2",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 9,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "If he will contend with him, he cannot answer him one of a thousand.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 18,
            "text": "Eccl. 6:10; Isa. 45:9; Ether 4:8."
          },
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 56,
            "text": "OR one time in."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
