        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 9:9",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 9,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "Which doeth great things past finding out; yea, and wonders without number.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 9:10",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 9,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "Lo, he goeth by me, and I see him not: he passeth on also, but I perceive him not.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 30,
            "end": 33
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 9:11",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 9,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "Behold, he taketh away, who can hinder him? who will say unto him, What doest thou?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 72,
            "end": 77,
            "text": "Rom. 9:20 (20–21); Moses 1:4."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 9:12",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 9,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "If God will not withdraw his anger, the proud helpers do stoop under him.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 2
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 9:13",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 9,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "How much less shall I answer him, and choose out my words to reason with him?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 34,
            "end": 37
          },
          {
            "start": 58,
            "end": 67
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 9:14",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 9,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "Whom, though I were righteous, yet would I not answer, but I would make supplication to my judge.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 85,
            "end": 96,
            "text": "OR before my accuser."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 31,
            "end": 34
          },
          {
            "start": 55,
            "end": 58
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 9:15",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 9,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "If I had called, and he had answered me; yet would I not believe that he had hearkened unto my voice.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 44
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 9:16",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 9,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "For he breaketh me with a tempest, and multiplieth my wounds without cause.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 9:17",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 9,
        "verse": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "He will not suffer me to take my breath, but filleth me with bitterness.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 18,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 9:18",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 9,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "If I speak of strength, lo, he is strong: and if of judgment, who shall set me a time to plead?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 3,
            "end": 10
          },
          {
            "start": 28,
            "end": 33
          },
          {
            "start": 86,
            "end": 95
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 19,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 9:19",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 9,
        "verse": 19
      },
      {
        "text": "If I justify myself, mine own mouth shall condemn me: if I say, I am perfect, it shall also prove me perverse.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 54,
            "end": 63
          },
          {
            "start": 66,
            "end": 68
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 20,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 9:20",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 9,
        "verse": 20
      },
      {
        "text": "Though I were perfect, yet would I not know my soul: I would despise my life.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 23,
            "end": 26,
            "text": "HEB I regard not myself."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 6
          },
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 13
          },
          {
            "start": 23,
            "end": 26
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 21,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 9:21",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 9,
        "verse": 21
      },
      {
        "text": "This is one thing, therefore I said it, He destroyeth the perfect and the wicked.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 43,
            "end": 53,
            "text": "Mal. 3:14 (14–18)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 5,
            "end": 7
          },
          {
            "start": 12,
            "end": 18
          },
          {
            "start": 36,
            "end": 39
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 22,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 9:22",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 9,
        "verse": 22
      },
      {
        "text": "If the scourge slay suddenly, he will laugh at the trial of the innocent.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 38,
            "end": 43,
            "text": "HEB mock."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 23,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 9:23",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 9,
        "verse": 23
      },
      {
        "text": "The earth is given into the hand of the wicked: he covereth the faces of the judges thereof; if not, where, and who is he?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 108,
            "end": 111
          },
          {
            "start": 116,
            "end": 118
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 24,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 9:24",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 9,
        "verse": 24
      },
      {
        "text": "Now my days are swifter than a post: they flee away, they see no good.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 31,
            "end": 35,
            "text": "HEB runner."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 25,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 9:25",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 9,
        "verse": 25
      },
      {
        "text": "They are passed away as the swift ships: as the eagle that hasteth to the prey.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 54,
            "end": 58
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 26,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 9:26",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 9,
        "verse": 26
      },
      {
        "text": "If I say, I will forget my complaint, I will leave off my heaviness, and comfort myself:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 81,
            "end": 88
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 27,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 9:27",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 9,
        "verse": 27
      },
      {
        "text": "I am afraid of all my sorrows, I know that thou wilt not hold me innocent.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 28,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 9:28",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 9,
        "verse": 28
      },
      {
        "text": "If I be wicked, why then labour I in vain?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 2
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 29,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 9:29",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 9,
        "verse": 29
      },
      {
        "text": "If I wash myself with snow water, and make my hands never so clean;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 30,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 9:30",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 9,
        "verse": 30
      },
      {
        "text": "Yet shalt thou plunge me in the ditch, and mine own clothes shall abhor me.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 31,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 9:31",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 9,
        "verse": 31
      },
      {
        "text": "For he is not a man, as I am, that I should answer him, and we should come together in judgment.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 9
          },
          {
            "start": 26,
            "end": 34
          },
          {
            "start": 56,
            "end": 59
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 32,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 9:32",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 9,
        "verse": 32
      },
      {
        "text": "Neither is there any daysman betwixt us, that might lay his hand upon us both.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 21,
            "end": 36,
            "text": "OR arbiter between."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 45
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 33,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 9:33",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 9,
        "verse": 33
      },
      {
        "text": "Let him take his rod away from me, and let not his fear terrify me:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 47,
            "end": 55,
            "text": "HEB the dread of Him."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 34,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 9:34",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 9,
        "verse": 34
      },
      {
        "text": "Then would I speak, and not fear him; but it is not so with me.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 4
          },
          {
            "start": 42,
            "end": 47
          }
        ],
